From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Blake <chrisrblake93@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:45:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] board: ulanzi: d200: pick the panel at boot

The D200 has one of two panels, which need different timings and init
sequences: the one rk3308-ulanzi-d200.dts describes ("h1"), or the one
of the rk3308-ulanzi-d200-panel-h3 overlay ("h3"). Pick it before the
display is probed, in this order:

- the "panel" env variable, if it is h1 or h3 (unset or "auto": detect).
  It is kept in the saved env (ENV_FLAGS_LIST_STATIC), so Linux can set
  it with fw_setenv;
- the panel's own registers, read over its 3-wire SPI link and matched
  against a table. No register is known to tell the panels apart yet,
  so the table is empty;
- the SoC variant, by RAM size: 128 MiB (RK3308H1) usually comes with
  the h1 panel, 256 MiB (RK3308H3) with the h3 one;
- otherwise h1.

For h3 the overlay, built into U-Boot, is applied to the live control
DT, so the boot logo already uses it. The choice goes to the boot script
as d200_panel: Linux boots the FIT configuration of that name, which
applies the same overlay, and gets d200.panel= on its command line. A
FIT image without that configuration boots its default one.

To find registers that identify the panel, page 1 registers 0x78-0x7e
are read at every boot after a reset of the panel, printed and passed to
Linux as d200.panel_regs=. This adds about 0.2 s to the boot.

Signed-off-by: Chris Blake <chrisrblake93@gmail.com>
---
 board/ulanzi/d200/Makefile           |   8 +-
 board/ulanzi/d200/d200.c             |   5 +-
 board/ulanzi/d200/panel.c            | 281 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 board/ulanzi/d200/panel.h            |   8 +
 board/ulanzi/d200/ulanzi-d200.env    |  22 ++-
 configs/ulanzi-d200-rk3308_defconfig |   2 +-
 6 files changed, 316 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 board/ulanzi/d200/panel.c
 create mode 100644 board/ulanzi/d200/panel.h

